---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import FinalCTA from '@/components/FinalCTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Inventing Creator-Led Sports Broadcasting with Thursday Night Football"
  description=""
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="cs-hero section">
  <div class="cs-hero-inner">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">— Case Study</span>
      <h1>Inventing Creator-Led Sports Broadcasting with Thursday Night Football</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-desc">
        Traditional sports broadcasts were fundamentally passive. I led the strategy for Thursday Night Football on Twitch — pioneering the creator co-streaming format that reimagined live sports through real-time community interaction. Years later, this model became the industry standard.
      </p>
      <div class="cs-hero-meta">
        <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Company</span>
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">Twitch / Amazon / NFL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Industry</span>
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">Sports &amp; Entertainment</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Scope</span>
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">National</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Focus</span>
          <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">Format Innovation &amp; Growth</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero-image">
          <img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d84514_01cfbac252c841b193b4fbcf0491dff0~mv2.png" alt="Thursday Night Football marketing" />
        </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs-results-strip section">
  <div class="cs-results-strip-inner">
    <div class="cs-result-stat">
      <div class="cs-stat-num">3.3M</div>
      <div class="cs-stat-label">Hours Watched</div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-result-stat">
      <div class="cs-stat-num">+73%</div>
      <div class="cs-stat-label">YoY Viewership Growth</div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-result-stat">
      <div class="cs-stat-num">128M+</div>
      <div class="cs-stat-label">Impressions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-result-stat">
      <div class="cs-stat-num">70-74%</div>
      <div class="cs-stat-label">Audience Interaction Rate</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs-section section">
  <span class="eyebrow">— The Situation</span>
  <h2>Sports Broadcasting Hadn't Embraced Creator Culture</h2>
  <p>
    Twitch had established itself as the global leader in live gaming content, but the next phase required expanding beyond gaming. Sports presented a major opportunity — the overlap between gaming and sports audiences was significant, yet traditional broadcasts remained fundamentally passive. No one had embraced creator-driven commentary formats for live sports.
  </p>
  <div class="cs-challenge-grid">
    <ul class="cs-challenge-list">
      <li class="cs-challenge-item">
        <div class="cs-challenge-num">1</div>
        <div class="cs-challenge-text">
          <strong>No proven model for creator-led sports broadcasts.</strong> The format that would later become the Manningcast and other alternate broadcasts simply didn't exist yet — it needed to be invented.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="cs-challenge-item">
        <div class="cs-challenge-num">2</div>
        <div class="cs-challenge-text">
          <strong>Traditional sports media was entirely passive.</strong> Fans watched games with professional commentators, with no way to interact, participate, or shape the viewing experience.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="cs-challenge-item">
        <div class="cs-challenge-num">3</div>
        <div class="cs-challenge-text">
          <strong>Twitch needed to prove sports could work on the platform.</strong> Demonstrating that live sports could thrive inside a creator ecosystem was essential for Twitch's expansion beyond gaming.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="cs-challenge-item">
        <div class="cs-challenge-num">4</div>
        <div class="cs-challenge-text">
          <strong>The NFL partnership demanded results at scale.</strong> Working with the NFL and Amazon required a format that could deliver meaningful viewership, not just an experiment.
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="cs-callout">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--green-lt)">— The Mandate</span>
      <blockquote>
        Prove that live sports could succeed on a creator-driven platform — and develop a new broadcast format that blended traditional sports with interactive community experiences.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="cs-approach section">
  <div class="cs-section-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">— The Approach</span>
    <h2>Reimagining Sports Through Community Interaction</h2>
    <p>
      We invented the creator co-streaming model: creators broadcast the live game to their own communities while adding commentary, reactions, and chat interaction. Fans could watch with their favorite creator, inside a live chat, with commentary that felt authentic and conversational.
    </p>
    <div class="cs-phases">
      <div class="cs-phase-card">
        <div class="cs-phase-num">01</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-title">Inventing the Creator Co-Stream</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-desc">
          Pioneered the format where creators layered their personalities and communities on top of the live game broadcast. Fans watched with their favorite creator inside live chat with authentic, conversational commentary.
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/content-creator-marketing" class="cs-phase-tool">Content &amp; Creator Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-phase-card">
        <div class="cs-phase-num">02</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-title">Scaling the Creator Ecosystem</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-desc">
          Built a program integrating 21 creators and 200+ streams across the NFL season. Expanded to include Spanish and German language broadcasters and professional athlete guest co-streams.
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="cs-phase-tool">Go-to-Market Strategy →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-phase-card">
        <div class="cs-phase-num">03</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-title">Integrated Marketing Engine</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-desc">
          Built a full-funnel campaign across owned channels (front page, push, email) and paid media (search, social, programmatic) driving 128M+ impressions and 581K clicks.
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/integrated-marketing" class="cs-phase-tool">Integrated Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-phase-card">
        <div class="cs-phase-num">04</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-title">Interactive Viewing Mechanics</div>
        <div class="cs-phase-desc">
          Integrated Twitch-native features including real-time chat, viewer prediction extensions tied to gameplay, and community participation mechanics — driving 70-74% audience interaction rates.
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/growth-marketing" class="cs-phase-tool">Growth &amp; Lifecycle Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="cs-ba section">
  <div class="cs-ba-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">— Transformation</span>
    <h2>Before &amp; After TNF on Twitch</h2>
    <div class="cs-ba-grid">
      <div class="cs-ba-before">
        <div class="cs-ba-label">Before</div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">Sports broadcasts were entirely passive — one-way, professional commentary only</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">No creator-led sports formats existed in mainstream media</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">Fan engagement limited to watching and social media commentary</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">No proven model for interactive live sports viewing</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-ba-after">
        <div class="cs-ba-label">After</div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">Creator co-stream format invented — fans watch with their favorite creators</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">21 creators, 200+ streams, multilingual coverage across the NFL season</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">70-74% audience interaction rates through predictions and chat</div></div>
        <div class="cs-ba-item"><div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div><div class="cs-ba-text">Format later adopted industry-wide — Manningcast, creator watch parties, and more</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs-results section">
  <div class="cs-results-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">— Results</span>
    <h2>The Numbers Tell the Story</h2>
    <p>A format-defining program that proved creator-led sports broadcasting could work at scale.</p>
    <div class="cs-results-grid">
      <div class="cs-result-card">
        <div class="cs-result-metric">3.3M</div>
        <div class="cs-result-label">Total Hours Watched</div>
        <div class="cs-result-desc">3.3 million hours of Thursday Night Football programming watched during a single season on Twitch, demonstrating massive demand for interactive sports viewing.</div>
        <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:90%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-card">
        <div class="cs-result-metric">+73%</div>
        <div class="cs-result-label">YoY Viewership Growth</div>
        <div class="cs-result-desc">Year-over-year growth in hours watched for the program, proving the format was gaining momentum and building a loyal audience each season.</div>
        <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:85%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-card">
        <div class="cs-result-metric">128M+</div>
        <div class="cs-result-label">Impressions Generated</div>
        <div class="cs-result-desc">Marketing campaigns drove over 128 million impressions with 581K clicks and 1.1M hours watched attributed to marketing channels across the season.</div>
        <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:80%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-card">
        <div class="cs-result-metric">70-74%</div>
        <div class="cs-result-label">Audience Interaction Rate</div>
        <div class="cs-result-desc">Prediction extensions alone drove 70-74% audience interaction rates, far exceeding engagement seen in any traditional sports broadcast format.</div>
        <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:95%"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs-impact section">
  <span class="eyebrow">— Impact</span>
  <h2>The Birth of a New Sports Broadcasting Format</h2>
  <p>
    The most important outcome was not just viewership — it was the creation of a new sports broadcasting format. The creator co-stream model pioneered on Twitch proved that sports fans wanted commentary that felt conversational, interactive, and community-driven.
  </p>
  <p>
    Today, that model has been widely adopted across sports media, from alternate broadcasts to influencer-led watch parties. Thursday Night Football on Twitch was the first large-scale proof that creator-led sports broadcasting could work — years before formats like the Manningcast normalized the idea.
  </p>
  <div class="cs-impact-callout">
    <div class="cs-impact-icon">🏈</div>
    <div class="cs-impact-text">
      The creator co-stream format invented for Thursday Night Football on Twitch became the blueprint for interactive sports broadcasting — a model now replicated across the industry by ESPN, the NFL, and major sports properties worldwide.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs-services section">
  <span class="eyebrow">— Capabilities Applied</span>
  <h2>What This Took</h2>
  <div class="cs-services-pills">
    <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="cs-service-pill">Go-to-Market Strategy</a>
    <a href="/services/integrated-marketing" class="cs-service-pill">Integrated Marketing</a>
    <a href="/services/content-creator-marketing" class="cs-service-pill">Content &amp; Creator Marketing</a>
    <a href="/services/growth-marketing" class="cs-service-pill">Growth &amp; Lifecycle Marketing</a>
  </div>
</section>

<FinalCTA />


  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
